The big question about creating a bones level is whether you or not you
are playing on a public machine.  If this is the case, it will be very 
tough to make sure that your bones level is in your next dungeon (un-
less there is some way to do this w/ the code or whatever)--unless you
do it very close to the surface.  

Unfortunately, doing this close to the surface means that your fellow
nethackers have a chance of getting your stash.  Which would be great 
for them (heck, there's nothing better than finding a free grayswandir 
in my own opinion).  

One way could be to do what I was meaning to do with an amazing character
who (due to being a tourist in 'unfixed' 3.1.0--we have no games sysamdin 
to take care of these things) would have left his stuff behind--mostly a 
huge pile of gems that would add vital points to his prospective descen-
dants.  Unfortunately, some mixup w/ a Nurse crashed the dungeon.  The 
plan was to use Xorn shape (which I am a big booster of; is this, however,
an abuse too?) to bury everything very deep within the wall.  I didn't 
think at the time how my future character would retrieve said stuff but
hiding a Wand of Digging under a rock somewhere on the level could do 
the trick.  If you're mean, put all kinds of Engraved hints leading to 
the opposite side of the dungeon in which are a ton of rothes, orcs or 
other low-level killing critters, seeing that you don't want anyone 
else to survive with your bones level, whether or not they find your
stash and loot it.  

If you're on a PC, just plug away until you get the bones level.  How 
does one ensure that a bones level is created anyway, especially on a 
public machine?




